<title>RUSSIA: Russia 364-day T-bill yields avg 19.66 pct.</title>
<headline>Russia 364-day T-bill yields avg 19.66 pct.</headline>
<dateline>MOSCOW 1997-06-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>The annualised average yield on an issue of 364-day GKO discount Treasury bills (series 21077) was 19.66 percent at an auction on Wednesday, the Russian central bank said.</p>
<p>The 21076 bills, maturing on June 17, 1998, the closest maturity date to the new issue, on Tuesday closed at 83.80, to yield 19.71 percent.</p>
<p>Full details of the auction follow:  </p>
<p>    Series number		     21077</p>
<p>    Issue volume			8.00 bln rbls</p>
<p>    Denominations		     1.00 million</p>
<p>    Bids (nominal)		   10.76 trln rbls</p>
<p>    Bids (cash)			 8.94 trln rbls</p>
<p>    Sold				  7.87 trln rbls</p>
<p>    Proceeds			    6.58 trln rbls</p>
<p>    Average price		     83.61 pct</p>
<p>    Lowest accepted price	   83.53 pct</p>
<p>    Average yield		     19.66 pct</p>
<p>    Highest accepted yield	  19.77 pct</p>
<p>    Tenor				364 days</p>
<p>    Maturity date		    June 24, 1998</p>
<p>On Wednesday the Finance Ministry will also offer four trillion roubles in an additional 133-day tranche of series 22084 T-bills.</p>
<p>It will repay eight trillion roubles in a maturing issue of 231-day T-bills (series 22057).</p>
<p>--Moscow Newsroom, +7095 941 8520</p>
